      "updated_at": "2026-09-20T13:39:02Z",
      "body": "The library I was thinking of was [atomicwrites](https://github.com/untitaker/python-atomicwrites), which is archived in favor of [`os.replace`](https://docs.python.org/3.14/library/os.html#os.replace) or [`os.rename`](https://docs.python.org/3.14/library/os.html#os.rename). Those are both documented as atomic.\n\nThe simplest answer for lazy is probably to use `Path` instead of `File` param types, and handle opening the file yourself when you write. That's probably a lot simpler than all the stuff we have to go through for `File` anyway.",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
